I know I've been spamming the group a bit with these YAAPs, but with
this only being my second "proper" conduct ascension (unless you count
that weaponless monk) and my fastest ascension by a good 13k moves I
thought I ought to do a quick post for it. Oh, and it's also my first
non-human. :-)

Of course, using a priest for the atheism conduct is a bit of a cheat,
as you start off with holy water and inherently know if items are
blessed or cursed which at a stroke deals with two of the bigger
problems with going atheist. But priests aren't exactly perfect;
they're completely restricted skill-wise for many of the more usual
big-hitter weapon types, and with no divine gifts there was no way
around that. I stuck with the starting mace for quite some time, but
eventually wished for Grayswandir as probably the only usable artifact
weapon for a Chaotic priest, with sabres at least only being
restricted to Skilled.

I did quite a bit of spellcasting, which is definitely something I'll
have to do more of in future, I really like having that handy. The
magic mapping spell was directly responsible for cutting 10k moves off
my ascension time, and made Gehennom much less of a drag. I was also
surprised to get fireball down to a fairly-usable 27% fail towards the
end, though as a relatively expensive spell I only ended up using it a
few times. (Probably just as well, as I see I'd actually forgotten it
by the end!)

Wands of death were a problem, in an unusual way - I didn't see a
single randomly-generated one before the planes. Since I tend to lean
on those a bit on Astral (not being a big fan of using conflict
there), I used the wrest from the castle wand to get a second. The
third I found on Air.

Once I got to Astral, I got myself in a bit of trouble and found
myself hovering awkwardly around 60HP for some time, but luckily the
first altar was the right one. Having never worn life-saving, and
having managed to die on my last *three* ascensions (!), it was a big
relief to get rid of the Amulet. :-)


